Z||000000||martin1875||08-16-2001||11:31 PM||||i am thinking of instaling a 3.4 with the 84 4.10 transmission. what kind of 0-60 times do you have. this is gonna be my have fun fiero. i have an 85 se v-6 auto that i am gonna covert to the 3.4 / 4.10 combo. what i am looking for is a good off the line car and to have power when i want it in the curves. thanks for the help||||reg||1
Z||000001||banditbalz||08-17-2001||12:00 AM||||Sounds like a killer setup! should be good for pulling the front tires off the ground! I would guess 0-60 in aprox. 6 seconds.<BR>according to my timeslips, I am running 0-60 in 6.7 sec on a 2.8 with a stock geared 4 speed Muncie, K+N, and stock sized rear tires... <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/HardLaunch_5.jpg">  <P>------------------<BR>Silver 86 GT<BR>completely stock,<BR>completely fast!<p>[This message has been edited by banditbalz (edited 08-17-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||MooCow||08-17-2001||12:10 AM||||I have that setup and I love it.  I don't get why most people say that 4-speeds suck compared to the 5-speed.  I have driven the getreg, Isuzu, and I like mine the best with the Isuzu in close second.  As far as 0-60 times I dont have non, but I am sure it would be close to 6ish.  Also on the highway if you just tap the gas you fly.  First gear lauches hard but is sorta a waste, but second and third pull like crazy.  Hope this helps.<P>Thanks Ken<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig_7.jpg"> <BR>87 GT, 3.4 engine with a 4:10 tranny, and Viper Yellow!||||reg||6
